## fastcompile-macros 10: codegen: with 01373, write its one caller in blaze-macro-eval (fastcompile-macros is done and allows it)

Where: `crates/blaze-macro-eval/src/run.rs` `fn on_evaluator`, right after `eval.set_budget(..)` (line ~365).

What: when you land 01373 (`Evaluator::set_inherited_overflow_checks`), add in the same change:

```rust
if let Some(checks) = hir_ty_mir::mir::overflow::crate_checks_overflow(db, krate) {
    eval.set_inherited_overflow_checks(checks);
}
```

`krate` is already bound there (the macro crate). A proc-macro crate is never a lang crate, so this is always `Some`. Why: the compiled tier (`tier/build.rs` `policy`) and rustc both build inherited-check code (core `Sum`, `Step`, operator impls) with the macro crate's `-C overflow-checks`; without this the evaluator panics where a `--release` macro wraps.
